as licensed by the repository's LICENSE and COPYRIGHT.md.

Third-party library sources (versions and original artifact SHA-256 in dependencies.json):
 - jcifs-ng 2.1.10, AgNO3 GmbH & Co. KG and jCIFS contributors, LGPL-2.1-or-later.
   Source: https://github.com/AgNO3/jcifs-ng/tree/jcifs-ng-2.1.10
 - SLF4J API / NOP 1.7.36, QOS.ch, MIT.
   Source: https://github.com/qos-ch/slf4j/tree/v_1.7.36
 - Bouncy Castle 1.76, The Legion of the Bouncy Castle Inc., MIT.
   Source: https://github.com/bcgit/bc-java/tree/r1rv76
License texts accompany the plugin. Build script permits rebuilding/relinking
with replacement dependency artifacts (update dependencies.json accordingly).

Android compatibility modifications (2026-11-23): backport.py redirects
AutoCloseable to java.io.Closeable and Objects / StandardCharsets to the
plugin's equivalent helpers. Original downloaded artifacts remain unchanged;
the transformed binary is generated at build time. All modification sources
and build instructions are in plugins/file-browser in the nTv source tree.
The Bouncy Castle package is relocated under xiao.bu.channel.files.crypto.bc
to avoid Android's built-in BC classes. SmbCryptoProvider supplies a private
MD4 MessageDigest adapter for NTLM; no process-wide provider is installed.
